  "observation": "This benchmark estimates categorical choice frequencies: each sample adds Gaussian noise to a row of 21 utility means, selects a maximum, and increments that category. We compare all three source layouts, including global private workspace versus per-thread columns in shared memory. Every output probability is checked against an independent integer winner count and the probability-simplex identity. The finite shared sample is fixed across all models and reused across parameter rows. Agreement certifies that empirical operator for these inputs, not the error of the probability estimate relative to a Gaussian population or Monte Carlo convergence. Separate deterministic tie controls verify the actual policy: the final category wins a tied maximum; otherwise the earliest maximizing category wins.",
